      "id": "xc0arnl",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Meaning of Constitutional Amendment"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Article 368 in Part XX of the Indian Constitution deals with the powers of Parliament to amend the Constitution and its procedure.",
        "An amendment bill can be initiated only in either House of Parliament and not in the state legislatures.",
        "Amendments altering federal features require ratification by the legislatures of at least half of the states by a simple majority.",
        "There is no provision for holding a joint sitting of both Houses of Parliament if a deadlock occurs over a constitutional amendment bill.",
        "The President must give assent to a Constitutional Amendment Bill and cannot withhold or return it."
      ],
      "id": "bs61e2i"
    },
